Recommends: debsums, needrestart
Suggests: efibootmgr, dkms
Description: post-upgrade health report for Debian and Ubuntu
 pydebuprep inspects a Debian or Ubuntu system after a release upgrade
 (for example Debian 12 to 13, or Ubuntu 22.04 to 24.04) and reports on
 package state, APT sources, configuration file conflicts, the running
 kernel, bootloader, systemd units and timers, logs, mounts and disk space.
 .
 It is strictly read-only: it never changes the system, and every finding
 comes with the commands to fix it. An optional snapshot taken before the
 upgrade lets the report show what changed. Reports are available as text,
 JSON, YAML, HTML and Markdown, with exit codes suited to automation such
 as Ansible.
